course: dictionary
lesson: 3634
title: Fingerspelling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fingerspelling means spelling out a word letter by letter, using hand shapes. It is part of sign language. «Fingerspell your name» means make the hand shape for each letter of your name, one after another.
explain: People use fingerspelling for names, places and words that do not have a sign of their own. Ella's name has four letters, so it takes four hand shapes, one for each letter.
explain: Sign languages differ around the world. «BSL fingerspelling uses two hands, ASL fingerspelling uses one.» British Sign Language uses two hands for the alphabet, and American Sign Language uses one. The same word can look different depending on where you learn it.
fact: Fingerspelling means spelling out words letter by letter with hand shapes.
fact: Fingerspelling is part of sign language, used by deaf people and by the people who sign with them.
fact: Fingerspelling is used for names, places and words that have no sign of their own.
fact: «BSL fingerspelling uses two hands» and «ASL fingerspelling uses one hand».
fact: Fingerspelling is a noun, and the verb is fingerspell: «fingerspell your name».
exercise: «BSL fingerspelling uses two hands, ASL fingerspelling uses one.» How many hands does ASL fingerspelling use? | *One | Two | Three | None
exercise: What is fingerspelling used for? | Counting money | *Spelling names and words that have no sign of their own | Telling the time | Making music with the fingers
exercise: Ella wants to show her name in sign language. What should she do? | Sing it loudly | Write it on a board in capitals only | Point at the sky | *Fingerspell it, letter by letter
test: Which verb means to spell a word letter by letter with hand shapes? | Whisper | *Fingerspell | Sign | Translate
test: «Fingerspell your name» means what? | Sign your name on a form | Write your name in joined-up writing | Say your name very loudly | *Spell your name letter by letter with hand shapes
exam: What is the difference between BSL and ASL fingerspelling? | BSL uses one hand and ASL uses two | Both use one hand | *BSL uses two hands and ASL uses one | Both use two hands
